  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Verify proves workflow logic",
      "items": [
        "POST /api/verify runs synthetic fixture suites through the workflow/rules path with Mock providers.",
        "Each case gets a fresh SQLite :memory: repository that closes after the case; all cases run in the API process.",
        "Memory SQLite is not process isolation. Verify does not call Ollama or write Auth PostgreSQL or persistent Judge Demo plans."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Judge Demo persistence is separate",
      "items": [
        "Maker/Checker demo plans use MockVLMProvider and the separate Judge Demo SQLite file.",
        "Root Render config places that file on ephemeral storage. It is not the Auth PostgreSQL database.",
        "There is no connection from the Verify mock path to Ollama; these results do not prove production inference quality."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
